# Logs
# 🔴 `/logs` (leading slash) is deliberate: a bare `logs` pattern matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, so it silently swallowed
# `src/features/admin/logs/` — the whole admin logs screen. `git status` showed
# nothing, `git add src/features/admin/` skipped it without a word, and the
# build only failed after deploy (TS2307: cannot find module). Anchoring it to
# the repo root keeps real log directories ignored without touching source.
/logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Environment — real values never committed
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Editor
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Test / build caches
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
.chrome-tmp

# Vitest writes these while loading its config; they must never be committed.
vitest.config.ts.timestamp-*.mjs

# QA evidence — regenerable screenshots and JSON reports, not source.
# `outputs/*.md` (the written reports) ARE committed; the images are not.
qa/
harness/
outputs/qa/

# Stray debug screenshots left at the repo root by an earlier session.
restored-*.png

# Temp headless-Chrome probe profiles (verification scripts)
.chrome-probe*/
.admin-verify/
